      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2023311031,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The links there mostly seem to be talking about something different, that a `#` inside a name which is *not* a fragment identifier needs to be escaped, or else that Win32 ShellExecute will strip out everything after the `#`. We're using it as a fragment identifier so we're not getting the same problem as mentioned there.  In that case there wouldn't be any point in us doing it too, as it would be no better or worse than letting Win32 ShellExecute strip it.\n\nHowever, on Windows 11 I also see that having a `#` causes problems opening, but it's completely different from what is described in those links.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
