        {
          "id": 2025421589,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@chuckcraft \n\nIn [MainApplication::helpTopicAction](ui/qt/main_application.cpp#L307), try\n\n`QDesktopServices::openUrl(QUrl(QDir::fromNativeSeparators(url)))`\n\nI believe there's a problem that has to do with the presence of the fragment upsetting the auto detection (whether by Qt or Windows) of the native path separator. Transforming the string containing the directory to use forward slashes instead of backslashes makes it work with fragments.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
