        {
          "id": 2026326571,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "(I renamed `Wireshark User's Guide` to `WSUG` on dev machine to get rid of `%20` for testing)  \n  \nCould it be the handler for `file:` ? It seems to lop off the fragment.  \n\"C\" code and the resulting URL in the browser tabs.    \n\n`QDesktopServices::openUrl(QUrl(\"file:///C:/Development/wsbuild64/run/Debug/WSUG/ChTelLTE.html#ChTelLTEMACTraffic\"));`\n\n`file:///C:/Development/wsbuild64/run/Debug/WSUG/ChTelLTE.html`\n  \n`QDesktopServices::openUrl(QUrl(\"https://C/Development/wsbuild64/run/Debug/WSUG/ChTelLTE.html#ChTelLTEMACTraffic\"));`\n\n`https://c/Development/wsbuild64/run/Debug/WSUG/ChTelLTE.html#ChTelLTEMACTraffic`\n  \n`QDesktopServices::openUrl(QUrl(\"https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html_chunked/ChTelLTE.html#ChTelLTEMACTraffic\"));`\n  \n`https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html_chunked/ChTelLTE.html#ChTelLTEMACTraffic`",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
